From 8e09193417d07fdf39bc5ef2868f9f1770639246 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: onlyfish <linotfish@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:42:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] audiopolicy: read the 360RA flag from an audio_prop

vendor.360ra.effect is vendor_default_prop; audioserver is coredomain and
may not read it, so sony360RaEnabled() always saw an empty value and
disabled the 360RA routing logic.

Relabelling the property is not an option either: audio_prop carries
core_property_type, and private/property.te neverallows reads of that
attribute from non-coredomain domains, which is exactly what the audio
HAL (hal_audio_default) needs for libtsrupmix/libtsrspatializer.

Keep vendor.360ra.effect for the HAL and read a system copy,
persist.audio.360ra.effect (audio_prop), from the policy.

Change-Id: Ibc17b2f2b191cd7b0b2a9ae10e37b6e542710188
---
 services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/Sony360RAudioPolicy.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/Sony360RAudioPolicy.cpp b/services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/Sony360RAudioPolicy.cpp
index 1a995d9..68a9676 100644
--- a/services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/Sony360RAudioPolicy.cpp
+++ b/services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/Sony360RAudioPolicy.cpp
@@ -49,7 +49,10 @@ uint32_t sonyChannelCount(audio_channel_mask_t mask) {
 
 bool sony360RaEnabled() {
     char value[PROPERTY_VALUE_MAX] = {};
-    property_get("vendor.360ra.effect", value, "");
+    // vendor.360ra.effect is vendor_default_prop, which coredomain (audioserver)
+    // cannot read. The effect libraries in the audio HAL keep using that one; the
+    // policy reads a system copy with the audio_prop label instead.
+    property_get("persist.audio.360ra.effect", value, "");
     return value[0] == '1';
 }
 
